page('/baby/4-6-months/','Baby classes 4–6 months: Infant 2','What to do with a baby at 4 to 6 months: familiar-object flashcards and parent-led talking activities with everyday objects, foods, animals and faces, in short calm sessions.',crumb([['Baby','/baby/'],['4–6 Months']])+heading('INFANT 2','4–6 months: first words and familiar things.','The Infant 2 class. Around this age babies babble back, reach for what they know and love hearing your voice name the world, so this lesson pairs familiar objects with simple, natural words.')+stagePageBody({chips:[['Age','4–6 Months'],['Class','Infant 2'],['Subjects','Talk, first words, listening']],stageLessons:[fwftLesson],subject:'Talk',soon:`<div class="fc-stage lesson-soon"><div class="fc-stage-pills"><span class="fc-age">Earlier stage</span><span class="fc-class">3–4 Months</span></div><h3>Start with Infant 1</h3><p>Colours and first objects live at <a href="/baby/3-4-months/">3–4 months · Infant 1</a>.</p></div>`}));
page('/subjects/talk/','Talk: baby language activities by subject','The Talk subject collects Kiddo.school classes that support your baby’s early language: naming familiar objects, listening to your voice and growing first words, from 4 months onward.',crumb([['Subjects','/subjects/'],['Talk']])+heading('THE TALK SUBJECT','Say it softly, say it again.','Talk is the subject behind your baby’s first words: hearing your voice, watching your face and connecting sounds with the things they see. Every Talk class is short, calm and designed to be led by you.')+talkBody());
