page('/toddler/2-years/','Toddler classes at age 2: Toddler 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 & 8','What to teach a 2-year-old: colors and shapes, matching and sorting, animals and vehicles with their sounds, feelings and emotions, and garden bugs — short parent-led classes with look-and-find games, sorting play, sound fun, feeling talk and garden friends from Kiddo School.',crumb([['Toddler','/toddler/'],['Age 2']])+heading('TODDLER 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 &amp; 8','Age 2: colors, shapes, matching, sorting, sounds, feelings and garden friends.','The Age 2 classes. Two-year-olds love to point, name, match, sort and make sounds, so these stages add big-button find-it games, matching play, sorting and sound play to the calm card classes — always parent-led, never a test.')+stagePageBody({chips:[['Age','2 Years'],['Class','Toddler 3, 4, 5, 6, 7 &amp; 8'],['Subjects','Colors, shapes, matching, animal &amp; vehicle sounds, feelings, garden creatures']],stageLessons:[csLesson,msLesson,anLesson,vhLesson,emLesson,gbLesson],subject:'Think &amp; Talk',extra:`<h2 class="lesson-classheading">Circle Time</h2><div class="fc-stages">${lessonStageCard(helloSchool,'Circle Time 1','Age 2')}</div><h2 class="lesson-classheading">Play &amp; create</h2><div class="fc-stages"><a class="fc-stage lesson-card-link" href="/toddler/2-years/my-work/"><div class="fc-stage-pills"><span class="fc-age">Age 2</span><span class="fc-class">At the desk</span></div><h3>My Work</h3><p>Draw &amp; Scribble and Trace &amp; Follow — two little creative activities at the classroom desk.</p><span class="fc-open">Open My Work <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a><a class="fc-stage lesson-card-link" href="/toddler/2-years/play-and-practice/"><div class="fc-stage-pills"><span class="fc-age">Age 2</span><span class="fc-class">At the toy shelf</span></div><h3>Play &amp; Practice</h3><p>Match It, Sort It and What’s Different? — three gentle games with the familiar learning cards.</p><span class="fc-open">Open Play &amp; Practice <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a></div><h2 class="lesson-classheading">My Classroom</h2><div class="fc-stages"><a class="fc-stage lesson-card-link" href="/my-classroom/"><div class="fc-stage-pills"><span class="fc-age">Age 2</span><span class="fc-class">The school room</span></div><h3>My Classroom</h3><p>Circle time starts on the rug — and the desk, the toy shelf and the school bag are close by.</p><span class="fc-open">Open My Classroom <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a></div><h2 class="lesson-classheading">Where next?</h2><div class="fc-stages"><a class="fc-stage lesson-card-link" href="/preschool/3-years/"><div class="fc-stage-pills"><span class="fc-age">Age 3</span><span class="fc-class">The next stage</span></div><h3>Preschool: Alphabet, Numbers &amp; Shapes</h3><p>Age 3 is ready when you are: twenty-six alphabet cards, ten counting cards, twelve shape cards and twelve color pairs with gentle games — the same calm school, one stage up.</p><span class="fc-open">Visit Age 3 <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></span></a></div>`,soon:`<div class="fc-stage lesson-soon"><div class="fc-stage-pills"><span class="fc-age">Earlier stage</span><span class="fc-class">18–24 Months</span></div><h3>Start with Toddler 2</h3><p>First concepts — big and small, up and down — live at <a href="/toddler/18-24-months/">18–24 months · Toddler 2</a>.</p></div>`}));
